WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.435
-Thank you, thank you,
thank you so much!

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.602
Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:06.439
We are here from Studio 6A
in New York City!

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.607
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.076
Thank you so much for watching.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.411
Thanks for being here.
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:15.848
Well, guys, it's been five days
since the election was called,

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.385
and President Trump
still has no plans to concede.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:20.587
Pretty soon,
we're going to need

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.322
Vladimir Putin
to stage an intervention.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.723
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.558
[ Russian accent ] "Look, it
actually isn't my birthday.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.461
We --
We're worried about you."

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.895
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:31.030
[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, we could be working

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.598
on the pandemic or the economy,

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.001
but instead, we had to lure
Trump out of the White House

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.569
like a cat
burrowed under the couch.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.570
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.806
Ss, ss, ss, ss, ss, ss!

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.907
Trump's pretty much refusing
to leave the house.

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:44.344
He's basically turning into
the old man from "Up."

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.079
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.680
"I should've put helium
in these balloons.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.483
Why --
Why did I choose water?"

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:54.119
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:55.454
Well, yesterday,
a reporter asked

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:58.224
President-elect Biden
about Trump's refusal to concede

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.592
and what it means
for the country,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.260
and here's what he had to say.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.764
-I just think it's an
embarrassment, quite frankly.

00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:07.667
-Trump heard that and was like,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.469
"That's what you thought
was embarrassing?"

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.870
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.406
"A porn star sued me."

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.974
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.974 --> 00:01:18.177
"What about when I tossed
paper towels like free throws

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:20.446
at the hurricane victims?

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:23.449
This is embarrassing?
Okay. Okay."

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:25.318
That's right, Biden called Trump
an embarrassment.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.986
Then he left the podium
and spent 20 minutes

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.088
trying to find
the opening in the curtain.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.356
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.693
"You gotta be kidding me."

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.663
But it's been a pretty rough
couple of weeks for Trump.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.932
Has there been
any good news for him?

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.901
-NBC News
has projected President Trump

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.002
as the winner
of the state of Alaska.

00:01:44.002 --> 00:01:49.042
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.844
-When the news broke,
Steve Kornacki was like,

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.579
"You woke me up for this?!"

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.579
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.148
"It's three electoral votes!"

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:59.953
Trump needs like 63
electoral votes, and he got 3.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.788
It's like asking your friend
for 20 bucks,

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.756
and they're like,
"I have a Canadian loonie."

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.825
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.459
But Trump appreciated
the victory.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:09.528
Today, he said,
"I want to thank Alaska

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.164
and their leader, Queen Elsa."

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.299
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.201
Well, this is interesting.
Most Republicans

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.169
haven't congratulated Biden
on his win,

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.405
but they have been talking
to his good friend,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.441
Democratic Senator Chris Coons.
Listen to this.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:24.810
-What are they telling you
behind the scenes?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.448
-Um -- [ Chuckles ] -- bluntly,
that they accept that --

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:32.584
I mean they call me to say,
you know, "Congratulations.

00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:35.521
Please convey my well wishes
to the President-elect,

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.824
but I can't say that
publicly yet."

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.158
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.726
-Is this the third grade?

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.127
It's like,
"Can you tell Emily

00:02:42.127 --> 00:02:43.796
that I have a crush
on her friend Ruby?"

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.931
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:47.934
Meanwhile, assuming Trump
does leave office,

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.436
the intelligence community
is worried that he might reveal

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.772
some of the country's
most classified secrets,

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:56.275
possibly in exchange for favors.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.210
It's already not a great sign
that the White House

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.647
Domino's guy is like,
"I know some things."

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:03.682
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:06.352
"I've seen some things."

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.787
Yeah, America's gone
from thinking,

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.488
"How could he not read
intelligence memos?"

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.824
to, "Thank God he didn't read
intelligence memos."

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.559
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.027
I wouldn't worry, though.
You know the Pentagon

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:17.096
probably made stuff up
just to see if he was listening.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:21.533
It's like, "Sir, this is
highly classified, but at night,

00:03:21.533 --> 00:03:23.436
the Natural History Museum
comes alive."

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.470
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:29.208
"What?!"
"Shh! Just don't tell."

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.210
Speaking of Trump's life
after the presidency,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.646
here's something that should
make him feel a little better.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:37.449
-President Trump could land
a $100 million book deal

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:39.285
about his time
in the White House.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.887
"The New York Post" reports
the President has been bombarded

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:44.190
with offers for book
and TV deals.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.358
The White House
has not commented.

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:48.594
-$100 million.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:51.063
When he heard that, Trump didn't
just concede, he quit.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:53.499
He's like, "I'm out.
It's 100 mil."

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.867
Meanwhile, Melania was like,

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.503
"Just when I thought I was out,
he pulls me back in."

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:01.206
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:03.909
$100 million is a lot,

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.445
'cause you know Trump's
just gonna print out

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.146
all his tweets
and staple them together.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.714
"Done. Pay me.
There you go.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:11.550
There's my book."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.652
In the meantime,
I read the Trump administration,

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:15.621
though, wants to make
the U.S. citizenship test

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:18.891
more difficult so it's harder
to become a citizen.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.693
They even had President Trump
try it out,

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.561
but I think they might have
made it a little too tough.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.330
I mean, check out his answers.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.298
For example,
when asked, "To win an election,

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:29.502
you need the most blank,"
Trump wrote down, "Lawyers."

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.437
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:34.139
Next, for the question, "Where
was the Constitution signed?"

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:37.409
Trump wrote down "Four Seasons
Total Landscaping."

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:40.146
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:44.383
What?

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:45.551
Not a good start.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.353
Next up, for,
"What is the U.S. motto,

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.088
which can be found
on the dollar bill?"

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.657
Trump wrote,
"Nobody out-pizzas the Hut."

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.692
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:55.694
So close.
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:58.898
Next up, for, "What did the
Declaration of Independence do?"

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:01.433
Trump put "Separated Harry
and Meghan from England."

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:02.768
I mean --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:05.938
Why would he keep taking
the test if he's --

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:08.174
But, up next,
"If the president

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.775
and vice president
can no longer serve,

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.010
who becomes president?"

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.079
Trump put down
"Colonel Sanders."

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.214
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.816
Next up, it says, "What does
the president's cabinet do?"

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:19.852
Trump said, "Hold
the president's snacks."

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:23.021
I mean, at this point,
he should stop taking the test.

00:05:23.021 --> 00:05:24.823
Why would they even have him --

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:28.427
But he continued
to answer more questions.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:31.430
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.266
For the question, "Who do we
thank on Veterans Day?"

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:37.136
Trump somehow wrote, "Doctors
who take care of animals."

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.772
That's not veterans.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.707
And finally, Trump answered
one more question

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:43.275
before they took away his pen,

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:45.043
for, "What is
the supreme law of the land?"

00:05:45.043 --> 00:05:47.579
He wrote, "Eat, tweet, repeat."
There you go.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:51.483
Actually he did better
than I expected.

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:54.053
Some business news.
I saw that Chipotle is opening

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.589
its first-ever
digital-only restaurant,

00:05:56.589 --> 00:06:00.459
where customers have to order
ahead and pick up their food.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:02.628
I'm just afraid,
because of these changes,

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:04.296
eating Chipotle
will no longer feel

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:06.199
like an authentic
Mexican experience.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:12.438
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.907
When the cashier calls out,
"Steak burrito for Greg!"

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:17.677
a lot of customers will be like,
"Whoa! How did you know?"

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.078
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.279
Here's some more tech news.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:22.882
Uber is launching a new feature.
Check this out.

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:25.250
-Uber is launching a new service
to try to attract

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.386
more customers
during the pandemic.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.889
The new option
is called Uber Reserve.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:32.959
Customers can now reserve rides
up to 30 days in advance,

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:37.063
and they can pick their favorite
driver for the trip.

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.664
-Who has a favorite Uber driver?

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:41.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.303
It's like having a favorite
subway conductor.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.205
Now Uber drivers are gonna be
the ones thinking,

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:47.707
"I hope this guy
doesn't murder me."

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:49.408
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:52.044
Also, 30 days?
Who's like, "Okay.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:54.046
I'm gonna be drunk in Brooklyn
on a street corner

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:57.482
30 days from right now"?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.482 --> 00:07:00.219
And, finally, in Spain,
a 19-year-old climber

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:03.488
made it to the top
of a 660-foot crane

00:07:03.488 --> 00:07:05.658
and then decided
to hang out naked.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.360
Here's the photo.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.062
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.964
Everyone on the street below
was like, "That guy's nuts!"

00:07:12.964 --> 00:07:15.568
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:18.303
[ Rim shot ]

00:07:18.303 --> 00:07:20.573
When people told him no one
wants to see his testicles,

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:21.807
he was like, "In Spain,

00:07:21.807 --> 00:07:23.809
it's actually pronounced
'tethicles.'"

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:26.212
[ Laughter and applause ]

